<!-- ========== SECTION 2: YEARLY DISTRIBUTION ========== -->
<section id="yearly-distribution" class="section">
  <h2>2. Year-by-Year Question Volume Analysis</h2>
  <p>The examination has not maintained a single fixed structure across all years. Instead, three distinct structural eras emerge, differentiated primarily by the number of Short questions.</p>

  <h3>Three Structural Eras</h3>
  <div class="era-row">
    <div class="era-block">
      <h4>Era 1: Foundation</h4>
      <div class="era-years">2015&ndash;2016</div>
      <div class="era-detail">
        <strong>27 questions/year</strong><br>
        15 MCQs + 9 Short + 3 Long<br>
        <span class="badge badge-stable">Baseline structure</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="era-block active">
      <h4>Era 2: Expansion</h4>
      <div class="era-years">2017&ndash;2019</div>
      <div class="era-detail">
        <strong>36 questions/year</strong><br>
        15 MCQs + 18 Short + 3 Long<br>
        <span class="badge badge-up">+33.3% from Era 1</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="era-block">
      <h4>Era 3: Stabilization</h4>
      <div class="era-years">2021&ndash;2025</div>
      <div class="era-detail">
        <strong>33 questions/year</strong><br>
        15 MCQs + 15 Short + 3 Long<br>
        <span class="badge badge-down">&minus;8.3% from Era 2</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout warning">
    <strong>2020 gap:</strong> No data exists for year 2020. This is consistent with widespread BIEK examination cancellations during the COVID-19 pandemic. All trend calculations treat this as a missing year, not a zero-question year.
  </div>

