  <h3>Year-over-Year Change Analysis</h3>
  <p>The data reveals a remarkably rigid structure within each era &mdash; once the BIEK sets a format, it holds perfectly year after year. Only <strong>two structural transitions</strong> occur across the entire 11-year span:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>2016 &rarr; 2017:</strong> Short questions doubled from 9 to 18 (+100%), driving total questions up by +33.3%. MCQs and Long questions were unchanged.</li>
    <li><strong>2019 &rarr; 2021:</strong> Short questions reduced from 18 to 15 (&minus;16.7%), dropping total questions by &minus;8.3%. The 2020 gap makes it unclear whether this change happened in 2020 or 2021.</li>
  </ol>
</section>

